In support of his submissions that the promise to pay a time barred debt as per Section 25 (3) of the Indian Contract Act is a fresh contract enforceable independently and the arbitration clause contained in the MOU dated 18.05.2006 is not binding, learned counsel for the petitioner relied upon the following decisions:
a) In the case of The Union of India (UOI) Vs. Kishorilal Gupta and Bros. reported in AIR 1959 SC 1362;
