39. The only possible legal view that could have been taken by the arbitrator from the evidence available on record is to hold that the claim of the respondent is hopelessly barred by the law of limitation for the following reasons:
https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis a) Exs.C6, C7 and C8 does not satisfy the requirements of Section 25 (3) of the Indian Contract Act which enables a claimant to seek enforcement of a time barred debt;
b) Exs.C6, C7 and C8 are vague and ambiguous in nature.

The MOU dated 18.05.2006 (Ex.C1) has also not been referred to in the alleged confirmation of balance said to have been issued by the petitioner through Exs.C7 and C8;
c) The alleged confirmation of balance through Ex.C7 has been signed by S.Rajasekar as a Marketing Executive for M/s.Saravana FoundationS Limited and not on behalf of M/s.Saravana Global Holdings Limited, the petitioner herein;
